From: krita.js contributors
Subject: [PATCH] core: include stdlib.h directly for getenv

qsimd.cpp calls getenv but relies on a transitive declaration. The
Emscripten 7.0.0 headers no longer provide it along this include path.
Include its defining header rather than altering the CPU feature logic.

Applies to: qtbase 6.10.2
Equivalent upstream fix:
https://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/e72d6e46282e476290e657a434ceeeaea40625f7
The local patch uses the C header spelling in Qt 6.10.2.

diff --git a/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp b/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
--- a/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
+++ b/src/corelib/global/qsimd.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "qalgorithms.h"
 
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
 #if defined(QT_NO_DEBUG) && !defined(NDEBUG)
